  "worked_solution": "Notice that the elements of our set\n\n$$\n\u2026,\\,\\frac{1}{4},\\,1,\\,4,\\,16,\\,64,\\,\u2026\n$$\n\nform a two-way infinite geometric sequence with a common ratio $r=4:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =4 \\\\  & =\\frac{(1)}{(\\frac{1}{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{4} \\\\  & =\u22ef\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting  ${a}_{1}=4,$ the $n$th term ${a}_{n}$ of our sequence for $n\\in Z$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =4\\cdot {4}^{n-1} \\\\  & =4\\cdot {4}^{n}\\cdot {4}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{4}\\cdot {4}^{n} \\\\  & ={4}^{n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can define our set using a constructive definition as follows:\n\n$$\nS={{4}^{n}\\,:\\,n\\in Z}\n$$",
